{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RESOLVED — merged + validated.\n\nRCA: public rebar.llm.review_ticket() was removed pre-1.0 (-> review_plan/review_code); two tests/external live modules still called it and were missed by the removal epic (external tests excluded from the Verified gate), so 4 Live External Integration lanes died with 'AttributeError: module rebar.llm has no attribute review_ticket'.\n\nFIX (Gerrit change 1800, merged as d38eb1c7a1): retargeted BOTH call sites to review_code (surviving op returning REVIEW_RESULT with runner/model/findings), NOT review_plan (returns PLAN_REVIEW_VERDICT with no top-level findings, cannot satisfy either test's assertions).\n - test_pydantic_review_ticket_opus -> test_pydantic_review_code_opus: drives review_code on the frontier/opus model with the four-pass gate enabled (REBAR_VERIFY_ENABLE_CODE_REVIEW=1). Preserves the opus param-handling intent (no temperature 400 on a real pydantic_ai run) + runner/model/findings asserts (finalize stamps cfg.model/runner).\n - test_llm_trace.py: drives review_code (gate enabled, ticket-addressed) as the Langfuse OTLP trace vehicle; result.get('findings') is not None preserved unchanged.\n\nVALIDATION:\n - Gerrit: LLM-Review +1 (PASS) AND Verified +1 (CI run 31854837190 SUCCESS) -> submitted.\n - Authoritative live workflow_dispatch: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31856166064\n     * external LLM (live anthropic): GREEN  * external LLM (live openai): GREEN  * langfuse tracing round-trip: GREEN\n     * external LLM (live bedrock): RED — but on an UNRELATED test only: test_completion_banking_behavior_0707::test_dense_completion_banks_and_terminates_in_two_of_three_trials (completion-verifier bug: _observe_trial.observed_upsert() got unexpected kwarg 'evidence_sufficient'). 17 passed / 1 failed on that arm; ZERO 'review_ticket'/'no attribute' occurrences anywhere in the bedrock log -> the original regression is gone and my retargeted opus test is among the 17 passed. Filed as discovered bug ulcerative-confined-blacklemur (9c7c-4844-f53c-4eac), linked discovered_from.\n\nAC status: no review_ticket calls in tests/external (only doc/comment mentions remain); both modules retargeted to a surviving op with matching contracts; live lanes validate the retarget (3 LLM arms + langfuse green running the retargeted tests; the lone red arm is an unrelated pre-existing defect). Closing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786757604914945001,"uuid":"c62fbd99-f598-49b0-b360-5b24fe148772"}